.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt SINIT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sinit
.Nd tiny init
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a minimal init for Linux and BSD, an improved version of the sinit
from suckless.org.
It must run as PID 1 and exits with status 1 otherwise.
.Pp
On startup
.Nm
changes the working directory to
.Pa / ,
makes sure that file descriptors 0, 1 and 2 are open
.Pq Pa /dev/console ,
falling back to
.Pa /dev/null ,
sets
.Ev PATH
if it is unset, blocks all signals and runs the init command
.Pq Pa /bin/rc.init
in a new session.
After that it waits for signals and reaps zombie processes.
As a safety net, zombies are also reaped every 30 seconds.
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width "SIGUSR1, SIGUSR2, SIGPWR"
.It Dv SIGUSR1 , Dv SIGUSR2 , Dv SIGPWR
Power off the system.
Runs
.Pa /bin/rc.shutdown poweroff .
.It Dv SIGTERM , Dv SIGINT
Reboot the system.
Runs
.Pa /bin/rc.shutdown reboot .
On Linux
.Dv SIGINT
is sent by the kernel on Ctrl-Alt-Del when the
.Sy MOD_CAD
module is enabled.
.It Dv SIGCHLD
Reap terminated children.
.El
.Pp
All other signals are ignored.
While a shutdown is in progress further shutdown requests are ignored.
.Sh MODULES
Modules are enabled at compile time in
.Pa config.h .
With no modules enabled
.Nm
behaves like the original sinit.
.Bl -tag -width "MOD_NATIVE_SHUTDOWN"
.It Sy MOD_NATIVE_SHUTDOWN
When the shutdown command exits, fails to start, or does not finish within
.Dv SHUTDOWN_TIMEO
seconds,
.Nm
sends
.Dv SIGTERM
to all processes, waits up to
.Dv KILL_TIMEO
seconds, sends
.Dv SIGKILL ,
calls
.Xr sync 2
and then
.Xr reboot 2 .
The shutdown script no longer needs to power the machine off itself.
.It Sy MOD_CAD
Disables the kernel's immediate reset on Ctrl-Alt-Del
.Pq Linux ,
so that it is delivered as
.Dv SIGINT .
.It Sy MOD_RESCUE
If the init command fails to start or exits with a non-zero status, a
rescue shell is started instead of leaving the system without a console.
.It Sy MOD_RESPAWN
Keeps a list of services running, for example
.Xr getty 8 .
Services are started after the init command has exited and restarted when
they die, at most once every
.Dv RESPAWN_DELAY
seconds.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/bin/rc.shutdown"
.It Pa /bin/rc.init
Run once at boot.
Should mount filesystems and start daemons, then exit.
.It Pa /bin/rc.shutdown
Run on poweroff and reboot with the argument
.Ar poweroff
or
.Ar reboot .
Should stop daemons and unmount filesystems.
.It Pa config.h
Compile-time configuration: commands, modules and timeouts.
.El
.Pp
The paths above are the defaults from
.Pa config.def.h .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits with status 1 if it was not started as PID 1.
Otherwise it never exits.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kill 1 ,
.Xr reboot 2 ,
.Xr sync 2
.Sh AUTHORS
Based on sinit from suckless.or